Found in the binary spike (Getty/mcp-wiki-binary-spike, packed with PAR::Packer).

lib/MCP/Wiki/Server.pm:106 warns "Git is not available, the wiki is served without history and commits: $reason\n". $reason is the caught error and still ends with Perl's " at FILE line N." — in a pp binary that is the PAR cache path ($TMPDIR/par-<hex>/cache-<sha1>/...Server.pm line 58), in a CPAN install the absolute @INC path.

Proposal: strip the location from $reason the way tool errors already are (see the comment near Server.pm:387 on Path::Tiny errors carrying " at FILE line N."), and pin the wording in t/62-git-startup-warning.t. Cosmetic, not a release blocker.

Now Task 2 of docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-03-binary-mcp-wiki.md; must land before the first release that ships binaries (binary users see the PAR cache path).

t/62 extended: exact warning string + unlike / at \S+ line \d+/. RED: warning ends with ' at .../lib/MCP/Wiki/Server.pm line 101.' (Carp reports the caller, Server.pm, not History.pm). Same RED without Git::Raw.

Server.pm: new _strip_location helper (regex moved out of _error_text), applied to the Git startup warning reason. prove -lr t/ and Git::Raw-less run green.

Done: Git startup warning drops ' at FILE line N.' via shared _strip_location in Server.pm; t/62 green, full suite green with and without Git::Raw.

